![completeness: Docs 11/17](../../badges/completeness/11.svg) ![stability: stable](../../badges/stability/stable.svg) ![category: Class](../../badges/category/class.svg) ![box: TBox](../../badges/box/boxtbox.svg) ![stereotype: SubKind](../../badges/stereotype/subkind.svg)

## Definition

A named\-emotion PROTOTYPE / region — a typical, idealized core\-affect appraisal SIGNATURE labelling one gmeow:EmotionType, expressed in the canonical core\-affect basis \(gmeow:coreAffectMetricPAD, so every prototype shares one metric basis\)\. 'Model up, don't mint': a named emotion is canonically a prototype/region \(this\) or a gmeow:AffectComposite, never an unanalyzed primitive\. A prototype is a communication/bridging anchor and a classification LANDMARK, NOT ground truth — named emotions stay OPEN and CONTESTED \(Principle 9\), and nearest\-prototype classification is a vantage\-relative claim under a declared metric, never a stored label \(Principle 12\)\. Distinct from an episodic gmeow:AffectVectorObservation of a felt state: its gmeow:vantage is the naming TRADITION \(gmeow:prototypeAuthority\), not a real bearer, and its gmeow:observedFeature is the gmeow:EmotionType, not an occurrent episode\.

